{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"f399b602fd4e2a972e842a2fa2e3a8bc2693c8ca60d57a26f216e85f23fc9364","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_f68449af51f8406f1ba378f58039ed4f1b5046f8a2b2084fea50dd83fae09560","overall_assessment":"The paper proposes a post-hoc disentanglement paradigm that extracts disentangled representations from pretrained GANs, addressing the hyperparameter sensitivity of existing end-to-end methods. The work demonstrates competitive performance on standard benchmarks and offers a practical alternative for representation learning, though its impact is primarily confined to the disentanglement and generative modeling communities.","paper_id":"VCAXR34cp59","paper_identity_sha256":"747b4f639a197c5879ca5f1abd69776ade4581660b7d41520e13c176c3bf4649","prompt_identity_sha256":"2a42c16a08cf0067980e89598b492a8e997a265aa5ce9f050b91b0b4580b8f25","raw_response_sha256":"2fdfee8bf9a88cfbad321f197b7c76ca79e37b06094cfe78ea3f967faa319960","request_identity_sha256":"24c7c0e1c5570d2a47f826477f419a526380e5189e8d56e4fccce7f4ba5c8d43","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"1d1a7ab72db31e0a7a9f8f29377b39dcede5d1d8e08487b09eb92d60597fc1ba","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-005","SRC-006"],"review_text":"The work addresses a significant challenge in representation learning: the difficulty of tuning hyperparameters for disentanglement regularizers in unsupervised settings. By proposing a post-hoc extraction method from pretrained GANs, the paper introduces a paradigm that may influence researchers seeking more stable and hyperparameter-free approaches to disentanglement. The bridging of controllable generation and disentanglement learning offers a unique perspective that could be applicable to other generative models.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-022","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates the utility of the proposed method in specific domains such as abstract reasoning and fairness. The use of established benchmarks like 3D Shapes and Cars3D, along with metrics like Modularity and MIG, provides a solid foundation for evaluating domain-specific impact. The method's ability to achieve competitive performance in these tasks suggests its potential for practical applications in areas requiring disentangled representations.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper reports that the proposed post-hoc disentanglement method achieves results on par with or outperforming existing state-of-the-art methods in terms of disentanglement metrics. The variance in results is noted to be smaller compared to VAE-based approaches, indicating greater stability. However, the improvements are not consistently superior across all datasets and methods, with some cases showing competitive but not dominant performance.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-027","SRC-033","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper discusses the fairness of the learned representations, evaluating the unfairness score and noting that the variance is smaller compared to VAE-based methods. This suggests a potential societal benefit in terms of more consistent and fair predictions. However, the paper does not extensively discuss broader societal impacts or risks, focusing primarily on technical performance and stability.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"a298fdd98d9e307f470fd70b55c5e17f535ac7d40c7bac58f7c3fac0f86f1d79","paper_id":"VCAXR34cp59","paper_ordinal":108,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"2fdfee8bf9a88cfbad321f197b7c76ca79e37b06094cfe78ea3f967faa319960","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"VCAXR34cp59","raw